  {
    "id": "video-Uew5BbvmLks",
    "title": "TED-Ed: manage your emotions",
    "level": "B1",
    "source": {
      "kind": "youtube",
      "videoId": "Uew5BbvmLks"
    },
    "lines": [
      {
        "text": "You and your friend need to ace Friday's exam to avoid summer classes,",
        "start": 6.6,
        "end": 11.6,
        "wordStarts": [6.74, 7.26, 7.34, 7.48, 7.86, 8.16, 8.34, 8.76, 9.3, 9.72, 10.1, 10.42, 10.78]
      },
      {
        "text": "and after a week of studying, you both feel confident that you pulled it off.",
        "start": 11.4,
        "end": 16.3,
        "wordStarts": [11.52, 12.06, 12.34, 12.5, 12.7, 12.9, 13.52, 13.72, 13.94, 14.2, 14.72, 15.18, 15.32, 15.6, 15.72]
      },
      {
        "text": "But when you get your grades back, they're much lower than the two of you expected.",
        "start": 16.4,
        "end": 20.9,
        "wordStarts": [16.5, 16.78, 16.9, 17.02, 17.14, 17.28, 17.62, 18.14, 18.42, 18.6, 19.08, 19.54, 19.66, 19.88, 20, 20.12]
      },
      {
        "text": "You're devastated. However, your friend doesn't seem too bothered,",
        "start": 21,
        "end": 25.3,
        "wordStarts": [21.1, 21.42, 22.4, 23, 23.14, 23.6, 24.08, 24.34, 24.6]
      },
      {
        "text": "and it's making you wonder why you can't shake this off like they can.",
        "start": 25.2,
        "end": 29.5,
        "wordStarts": [25.3, 25.6, 25.76, 25.94, 26.24, 26.56, 26.86, 27.08, 27.44, 27.68, 27.98, 28.34, 28.66, 28.84]
      },
      {
        "text": "But should you really be trying to look on the bright side,",
        "start": 29.4,
        "end": 32.8,
        "wordStarts": [29.56, 29.76, 29.94, 30.1, 30.32, 30.5, 30.9, 31.22, 31.46, 31.72, 31.84, 32.06]
      },
      {
        "text": "and is controlling our emotions even possible in the first place.",
        "start": 32.7,
        "end": 37,
        "wordStarts": [32.82, 33, 33.18, 33.66, 34.1, 34.54, 35.2, 35.76, 36, 36.1, 36.34]
      },
      {
        "text": "The answer to the last question is a definitive yes.",
        "start": 37.4,
        "end": 41.4,
        "wordStarts": [37.58, 37.76, 38.02, 38.22, 38.34, 38.64, 39.12, 39.66, 39.76, 40.3]
      },
      {
        "text": "There are numerous strategies for regulating our emotions",
        "start": 41.8,
        "end": 45.1,
        "wordStarts": [41.98, 42.1, 42.3, 42.74, 43.32, 43.68, 44.14, 44.4]
      },
      {
        "text": "and one framework to understand these techniques is called the process model.",
        "start": 44.6,
        "end": 49.9,
        "wordStarts": [44.76, 45.16, 45.36, 45.72, 46.06, 46.46, 46.72, 47.16, 47.86, 48.18, 48.5, 49]
      },
      {
        "text": "Psychologists use this tool to identify where and",
        "start": 50,
        "end": 53.5,
        "wordStarts": [50.18, 50.76, 51.26, 51.5, 51.78, 51.94, 52.44, 52.94]
      },
      {
        "text": "how to intervene in the process that forms our emotions.",
        "start": 53.1,
        "end": 57,
        "wordStarts": [53.22, 53.58, 53.84, 54.24, 54.68, 54.78, 55.1, 55.4, 55.84, 56.22]
      },
      {
        "text": "That process has four steps.",
        "start": 57.1,
        "end": 59.7,
        "wordStarts": [57.24, 57.52, 57.92, 58.42, 58.86]
      },
      {
        "text": "First, we enter a situation,",
        "start": 59.3,
        "end": 62.1,
        "wordStarts": [59.44, 60.48, 60.72, 61.02, 61.24]
      },
      {
        "text": "real or imagined, and that draws our attention. Then we evaluate or",
        "start": 62.1,
        "end": 68,
        "wordStarts": [62.28, 62.58, 62.82, 63.58, 63.74, 63.94, 64.34, 64.76, 66.18, 66.34, 66.54, 67.14]
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "video-G3hXvByzLHs",
    "title": "TED-Ed: be more persuasive",
    "level": "B2",
    "source": {
      "kind": "youtube",
      "videoId": "G3hXvByzLHs"
    },
    "lines": [
      {
        "text": "You can't give a powerful new idea to",
        "start": 5.6,
        "end": 9.1,
        "wordStarts": [5.79, 6.69, 7.11, 7.25, 7.39, 7.83, 8.11, 8.57]
      },
      {
        "text": "an audience unless you can learn how to explain it.",
        "start": 8.6,
        "end": 12,
        "wordStarts": [8.77, 8.93, 9.35, 9.79, 10.09, 10.27, 10.55, 10.81, 10.95, 11.37]
      },
      {
        "text": "Each step builds on what the listener already knows,",
        "start": 11.9,
        "end": 15,
        "wordStarts": [12.09, 12.39, 12.69, 13.11, 13.31, 13.45, 13.59, 13.89, 14.35]
      },
      {
        "text": "and metaphors and examples help show how the idea is pieced together.",
        "start": 15,
        "end": 19.2,
        "wordStarts": [15.17, 15.41, 15.91, 16.11, 16.63, 17.01, 17.29, 17.57, 17.75, 18.11, 18.27, 18.57]
      },
      {
        "text": "But if explanation is building a brand new idea in someone's mind,",
        "start": 19.3,
        "end": 24.1,
        "wordStarts": [19.43, 19.69, 20.27, 20.93, 21.39, 21.69, 21.95, 22.11, 22.37, 22.87, 23.03, 23.51]
      },
      {
        "text": "persuasion is something a little more.",
        "start": 24.2,
        "end": 27.3,
        "wordStarts": [24.33, 25.03, 25.67, 26.09, 26.41, 26.57]
      },
      {
        "text": "Persuasion means convincing an audience that their way of seeing something, their perspective,",
        "start": 27.5,
        "end": 32.8,
        "wordStarts": [27.67, 28.31, 28.71, 29.17, 29.51, 29.83, 30.09, 30.29, 30.55, 30.69, 30.95, 31.67, 31.87]
      },
      {
        "text": "isn't quite right. That means taking down the",
        "start": 33.3,
        "end": 37,
        "wordStarts": [33.41, 33.93, 34.23, 34.69, 35.57, 35.83, 36.25, 36.57]
      },
      {
        "text": "parts of their thinking that aren't working and rebuilding something better.",
        "start": 36.6,
        "end": 40.5,
        "wordStarts": [36.71, 36.97, 37.09, 37.21, 37.49, 37.73, 38.01, 38.33, 38.79, 39.17, 39.69]
      },
      {
        "text": "Psychologist Barry Schwartz gave a talk that changed the way his audience thinks about choice.",
        "start": 40.8,
        "end": 46.7,
        "wordStarts": [40.97, 41.65, 42.15, 42.65, 42.99, 43.19, 43.43, 43.63, 44.01, 44.23, 44.41, 44.65, 45.05, 45.47, 45.85]
      },
      {
        "text": "Many people are obsessed with maximizing choice.",
        "start": 46.8,
